# Workout quality is non-negotiable (HARD)

Personal Coach workout programming quality is the product. **Never trade it away.**

## Absolute rules

- Prefer a **slower, correct brick** over a fast, weak, or generic one. Extra wait time for the athlete is acceptable.
- Never ship **offline / local / stub / template workouts** as a substitute for real coach programming.
- Never shrink, strip, or “compact away” programming prompts, policy, or capability profiling (POL-016 / POL-018) just to save tokens, latency, or quota.
- Never route **generate_block / generate_week / generate_week_detail / revise_*** through a weaker backup model that lowers programming quality.
- Intake UX may change (pickers, English-only, question order). **Programming brain / system / policy for building workouts must stay high-quality.**

## When providers fail

- Fail loudly and **retry / wait**, do not fill the calendar with fake sessions.
- Rate limits and long timeouts are better than low-quality WODs.

## What “good” means (do not regress)

- Relevant strength / skill part + functional metcon (or clear intent) per training day
- Athlete-specific loads, scales, and formats from intake
- Real 5-week brick continuity — not empty stubs or copy-paste templates

## Conflict resolution

If any change would make workouts worse to fix UI, quota, or deploy pressure: **reject the change** or isolate it so programming quality stays intact.
